cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAG Evaluation Lab: Grounding, Citations and Regression Testing"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Akor
    given-names: George
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jupiter-Plantagenet/rag-evaluation-lab"
abstract: >-
  A self-directed research-engineering case study in evaluating document-grounded
  retrieval-augmented generation. The repository implements an inspectable
  evaluation and regression-testing harness rather than a chatbot: it separates
  retrieval, answer, grounding/citation and system metrics instead of reporting a
  blended quality score; keeps deterministic metrics apart from model-assisted
  ones and publishes grader-agreement figures for the latter; captures structured
  per-case traces; classifies failures under a fixed taxonomy; and converts
  confirmed failures into regression tests that run offline with no model
  credentials. A deliberately simple baseline pipeline is compared against an
  improved pipeline whose interventions were selected from an observed failure
  distribution on a development split and evaluated on a held-out split frozen
  beforehand. Evaluated on one synthetic corpus with one embedding model and one
  generation model; it is a case study, not a benchmark.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - evaluation
  - groundedness
  - citation verification
  - regression testing
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-06"
